@* The documentation rail: a filter box over grouped links, in the shape of a
   Fluent 2 NavDrawer - a rounded row per item, a subtle fill when selected, and
   a pill indicator on the inline start edge.

   Clicking any link also closes the mobile drawer; on desktop the class toggle
   is a no-op. That is the delegated listener in demo.js matching the links
   themselves - no attribute on the list, so a click on a group header or on the
   padding between items leaves the drawer alone - and no inline onclick, so the
   site works under a strict Content-Security-Policy.

   Each link sits in a .nav-item wrapper because the filter in demo.js hides
   entries by toggling a class on them: the wrapper's class is rendered once and
   never re-rendered, while a class written straight onto a NavLink would be
   overwritten the next time NavLink recomputes its own active state. *@

